# KSI-MLA-LET: Azure Activity Log Alert - NSG Changes
# Azure 5.2.3: Alert on create/update NSG
# Azure 5.2.4: Alert on delete NSG

META
    esp_id `ksi-mla-let-az-activity-alert-nsg-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-MLA-LET: Azure Activity Alert - NSG write monitored`
    description `Validates that an activity log alert exists and is enabled to detect creation or modification of network security groups, ensuring network access changes are tracked`
    author `security-team`
    tags `azure,activity-log,alert,nsg,network`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,NIST:AU-12,NIST:SI-4`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-LET`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `3`
    recommendation `Create activity log alert via az monitor activity-log alert create --name alert-nsg-write --condition category=Administrative and operationName=Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups/write --action-group <ag-name>`

    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Event logging for network security changes is validated by confirming an activity log alert exists (found=true) and is enabled (enabled=true) that monitors the Administrative category for Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups/write operations. The alert must have at least one action group configured to ensure notifications are delivered when NSGs are created or modified. NSG changes directly affect network segmentation and traffic flow controls.`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Changes to network security groups are logged and monitored through activity log alerts that trigger on networkSecurityGroups/write operations, providing real-time notification of network access control modifications.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT alert_nsg_write
        name `alert-nsg-write`
        resource_group `rg-example-eastus`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE st_alert_active
        found boolean = true
        enabled boolean = true
        category string = `Administrative`
        operation_name string = `Microsoft.Network/networkSecurityGroups/write`
        has_action_groups boolean = true
        action_group_count int >= 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_activity_log_alert
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF st_alert_active
            OBJECT_REF alert_nsg_write
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
